{"availability":"available","full":"houstudio/cdroid","name":"cdroid","description":"CDroid is an open-source, Android-compatible GUI framework built on C++11, designed for cross-platform embedded systems development.it is more friendly for android developers.","category":"Design","language":"C++","stars":91,"forks":30,"created":"2021-06-30T06:08:58Z","updated":"2026-09-23T00:38:46Z","license":"LGPL-2.1","branch":"master","homepage":"https://houstudio.github.io/cdroid/","topics":["achartengine","androidx","cairo","constraintlayout","drawable","embedded","flutter","fragment","graphics","gui","lvgl","navigation","recyclerview","wearable"],"demo":"https://houstudio.github.io/cdroid/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T21:25:00.612Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T21:25:00.612Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T21:25:00.612Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T21:25:00.612Z","stars":91,"forks":30}],"technologies":["Flutter"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Android's UI framework, faithfully ported to C++ — Android-quality UI on embedded devices with no Android runtime, and a readable mirror of AOSP internals you can actually learn from.","CDroid is a line-by-line C++ port of Android's Java UI SDK — android.widget, android.view, android.text, android.graphics.drawable, android.animation — built on top of Cairo (vector graphics) and targeting embedded systems (runs in as little as 32 MB of RAM). It is neither a wrapper around Android nor merely \"Android-inspired\": class names, member names, method signatures, and control flow track the AOSP sources closely enough that you can open the Android reference next to the C++ and follow along line by line.","If you can describe a UI in Android XML, you can run that same UI on a set-top box, an in-dash display, or an industrial panel — designed in Android Studio, rendered by Cairo, no JVM in sight."],"features":["Contact: QQ 1225012331 / WeChat: calfhou","100+ widgets & 50 drawables, API-compatible with Android — design them in Android Studio / Eclipse.","Full AndroidX ports: RecyclerView, ConstraintLayout + MotionLayout, FragmentManager + Navigation, Flexbox, CoordinatorLayout, ViewPager2.","Fragment + Transition framework, including shared-element transitions.","Binary AXML resources end to end — aapt2-compiled XML + resources.arsc packed into .pak archives, real resource ids in generated R.h, build-time resource overlay."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/houstudio/cdroid/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"1ffaa7159ac725b0aff91c131ed910bbe5d2b03d32d0f7f2a7b001fbad52568a","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T21:25:00.761Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T21:25:00.761Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Android's UI framework, faithfully ported to C++ — Android-quality UI on embedded devices with no Android runtime, and a readable mirror of AOSP internals you can actually learn from.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/houstudio/cdroid/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"After login pls run git pull to get new version of cdroid","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/houstudio/cdroid/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"1ffaa7159ac725b0aff91c131ed910bbe5d2b03d32d0f7f2a7b001fbad52568a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/houstudio/cdroid/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T21:25:00.761Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-23T00:38:46Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/houstudio/cdroid/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T21:25:00.762Z","hash":"1ffaa7159ac725b0aff91c131ed910bbe5d2b03d32d0f7f2a7b001fbad52568a","originalBytes":9315,"storedBytes":9315,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["cdroid","android","install","aosp","build","c++","make","run","alarmmanager","build.sh","cairo","directory","embedded","framework","git","port","porting","vcpkg","xxx","app","constraintlayout","drawables","each","how","mirror","motionlayout","real","